**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests`

**How to implement.** The constructor window holds its kit's studies and fit runs, read when the kit opens and when it reloads, and the five study messages of S11.1 become window messages that record what they answer (001 §P 'CreateStudy, AddExperimentsToStudy, OpenMaterial, SetParameterScope, LinkParameters … The same messages back the buttons'; 001 §O 'Study view'; the S11.1 mapper's note 'The study view that sends them is S11.5's'; .spec-md §4 'UI': every user step is a semantic Elmish message). It follows the items' precedent (step 223). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`: `OpenedKit` (steps 150, 223) gains `studies : Study list` and `fitRuns : FitRun list` after `items`, each documented in one line: the kit's studies as `readStudies ()` (step 359) orders them, and every study's fit runs, study by study in that order and each in stamp order (`readFitRuns`, step 384). The private `openedOver` reads them after the items; a refusal closes the kit and is the answer, as any failed read is (step 150). `withRebindings` keeps them. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) Before the model: `StudySurfaceState = { studyOpt : StudyName option; fitRunOpt : FitRunName option; newStudyName : ControlCaption; newStudyExperiments : ExperimentName list }` with `static member initial` (nothing chosen, an empty name, no experiment): which study and fit run the study surfaces show, and the New study form's typed name and chosen experiments; window state, never stored. (b) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `kitStudies : Study list`, `kitFitRuns : FitRun list` and `studySurface : StudySurfaceState` after `flowStep` (step 238), each documented in one line; `initWith` sets `[]`, `[]` and `StudySurfaceState.initial`. (c) The private function of a kit's content that `loadKit` and `ReloadKitChanges` share (steps 187, 223) takes the studies and fit runs after the items and sets `kitStudies` and `kitFitRuns`; it keeps `studySurface.studyOpt` when the kit still holds that study and otherwise chooses its first study, or none, and keeps `fitRunOpt` only when the kit holds that run. `loadKit` passes `opened.studies` and `opened.fitRuns`; `ReloadKitChanges` reads `readStudies ()` and each study's `readFitRuns` after `readItems ()`, an `Error e` keeping the model and the offer with step 187's text; `CopyChosenExperiments` (step 225) passes the model's own. A changed `.study-json` or `.fitrun-json` is offered for reload by step 130's check, because both are kinds of `KitFileKind.all` (step 123). (d) On the model extension holding `tryItemModelChoice` (step 263), each documented in one line: `member model.studyContext : StudyContext` (step 366) = `{ studies = model.kitStudies; experiments = model.experimentCollection.experiments; setups = model.kitSetups; items = model.kitItems; resolveMaterial = <…> }`, whose `resolveMaterial version` answers `model.materials.resolveVersion version`'s `Ok (Some entry)` as `Ok entry`, `Ok None` as `MaterialUnavailableErr` naming the version's GUID and number, and `Error e` as `MaterialUnavailableErr` of `e.caption`'s text (`ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:MaterialError.caption`); `member model.selectedStudyOpt : Study option`, the study of `kitStudies` that `studySurface.studyOpt` names; and `member model.studyFitRuns : FitRun list`, the `kitFitRuns` of that study, oldest first, `[]` without one. (e) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `StudyCommand of StudyMsg` (the study verbs' message and how a test sends one, 001 §P), `SelectStudy of StudyName`, `SetNewStudyName of ControlCaption` and `ToggleNewStudyExperiment of ExperimentName`. (f) Arms. `StudyCommand msg` goes through step 185's read-only guard first; then `msg.applyTo model.studyContext` (step 366): `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `The study was not changed — <e.describe>` and records nothing; `Ok study` is recorded through `{ kit = model.kit; imports = model.catalogueImports }.recordStudy study` (step 359), whose `Ok ()` replaces the study of that name in `kitStudies` or adds it, in `readStudies`' order, sets `studySurface.studyOpt` to it, clears the New study form after a `CreateStudy` and sets `kitStatus` to `None`, and whose `Error e` keeps `kitStudies` and sets `kitStatus` to `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. `SelectStudy name` sets `studyOpt` when `kitStudies` holds the name, and `fitRunOpt` to the last of its fit runs or `None`; otherwise it changes nothing. `SetNewStudyName` sets the form's name; `ToggleNewStudyExperiment` removes the name when the form holds it and appends it otherwise. These three write nothing. No other field, message or option is added; the surfaces that send them are steps 414-418. Tests. `KitOpeningTests` (step 150) gains `opening a kit reads its studies and their fit runs, and a study file that does not read refuses the open`: a kit holding the studies `QZ-LR` and `LR`, written through `recordStudy`, and two fit runs of `QZ-LR` written through `writeFitRun` (step 384), closed, answers `studies` `LR` then `QZ-LR` and `fitRuns` the two in stamp order when opened again read-write and read-only; a kit whose `Broken.study-json` the test writes as `{` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitFileRejectedErr _)` naming it, and its folder holds no `.oc/lock`. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs`, `module StudyWindowModelTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, the home of the window's study arms. Its kit is a folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, "StudyWindowModelTests", <a new GUID>)` opened read-write through `KitOpening.openKitAt` (step 150) over the Built-in import context, as `KitWindowModelTests` opens its kits (step 184), holding CPL1, CPL2 and the Phone recorded through `recordItem` (step 219) over `ItemDraft`s of the built-in circular-polarizer and intensity-detector models (CPL1's and CPL2's `c2.retardance` unknown from 1.5 within [1, 2], the Phone's `gain` unknown from 1000 within [100, 10000]), one setup `Bench` holding them through `recordSetup` (step 260) and E1 and E2 (Science) and E3 (Calibration) over it through `recordExperiment` (step 149), closed, opened again and loaded into `initInverse` through `loadKit` (step 152), the window's stores and its `catalogueImports` being one `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` set, as `StudyMessageTests`' are (step 366). `a loaded kit's studies and fit runs are the window's, and Reload reads a study another writer wrote`: with `QZ-LR` and one test-local fit run of it written before the load, `kitStudies` is `[ QZ-LR ]`, `kitFitRuns` the run and `studySurface.studyOpt` `Some QZ-LR`; after another writer (step 187's `KitProxy.create` over the folder) records the study `LR`, `CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnActivation` offers `LR.study-json` and `ReloadKitChanges` leaves `kitStudies` `LR` then `QZ-LR` with `QZ-LR` still chosen. `CreateStudy from the window records the study, selects it and clears the New study form`: `SetNewStudyName (ControlCaption "QZ-LR")`, `ToggleNewStudyExperiment` of E1, of E2 and of E3, then of E3 again, and `StudyCommand (CreateStudy (QZ-LR, [ E1; E2 ]))` leave `kitStudies` holding `QZ-LR` over E1 and E2, `readStudies ()` answering it, `studyOpt` `Some QZ-LR` and the form `StudySurfaceState.initial`'s. `a refused study message is told and records nothing, and a read-only kit takes none`: `StudyCommand (AddExperimentsToStudy (LR, [ E1 ]))` with no study `LR` sets `kitStatus` containing `the kit has no such study`; over the kit opened read-only, `StudyCommand (CreateStudy …)` is refused by the guard; in both, `kitStudies` and the folder's files are unchanged. `selecting a study shows its own fit runs, oldest first`: with `QZ-LR` and `LR` and two fit runs of each written before the load, `SelectStudy LR` gives `studyFitRuns` `LR`'s two, oldest first, and `fitRunOpt` the later; `SelectStudy` of an unknown name changes nothing. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the window holds studies, `OpenedKit` MUST carry the kit's studies and fit runs read at open, `loadKit` and `ReloadKitChanges` MUST set `kitStudies` and `kitFitRuns`, and `StudyCommand` MUST apply a study message over `model.studyContext` and record the answered study through `recordStudy`, telling a refusal and writing nothing under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `opening a kit reads its studies and their fit runs, and a study file that does not read refuses the open`, `a loaded kit's studies and fit runs are the window's, and Reload reads a study another writer wrote`, `CreateStudy from the window records the study, selects it and clears the New study form`, `a refused study message is told and records nothing, and a read-only kit takes none` and `selecting a study shows its own fit runs, oldest first`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.
